:??The Cold War?? According to U.S. Federal Law, it lasted officially 
from September 2, 1945 (the date the Japanese formally surrendered 
thus marking the end of World War II) to December 26, 1991 
(the date of the formal dissolution of the Soviet Union).

:??JF Kennedy?? The president of the USA at the beginning of the sixties.


:??The Cold War?? It refers to a period of strong hostility between 
the capitalist world and the communist world, during which period 
nuclear threat was imminent.


:??The Vietnam War?? The USA got involved because it feared the spread 
of communism.


:??The Civil rights movement?? The fight of the black population for 
equal rights in the USA.


:??The Vietnam War?? Officially it lasted from 1955 to 1973, however 
fighting intensified during the sixties and at the beginning of 
the seventies.


:??Nikita Khruschev?? The president of the Soviet Union at the beginning
 of the sixties.


:??The Civil rights movement?? The most well known hero is Martin Luther
 King who was assassinated in 1968.
